 # Adversarial Code Review
 
+## Output Style
+
+Write all findings terse. Drop articles (a/an/the), filler (just/really/basically/actually/simply), hedging ("might possibly", "it seems", "perhaps consider"), and pleasantries. Fragments OK. Short synonyms (big not extensive, fix not "implement a solution for").
+
+Preserve EXACTLY: code blocks, file paths, line numbers, identifiers, URLs, quoted error strings, and any normative verdict labels this skill defines (e.g. CONFIRMED / REFUTED / UNVERIFIABLE). Never paraphrase quoted MR/PR claims — quote them verbatim.
+
+One short paragraph per claim. No meta-narration ("Here is my review...", "I will now verify..."). No marker comments or banners indicating the style.
+
 Never trust the MR/PR description at face value. Verify every claim by reading the actual code.
 
 ## Methodology
